<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Forum Hadriani</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Municipium Aelium Cananefatium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Forum Hadriani was a Roman town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> delta, at modern Voorburg near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. The chief town of the Cananefates, it received market rights under the emperor Hadrian around 121 CE and later the status of a municipium. It was the northernmost Roman town on the European mainland and was largely abandoned in the late 3rd century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/forum-hadriani.jpg" alt="Forum Hadriani" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Erren · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ForumHadriani_loc.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
